WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.680
- 2020 Is finally coming to a close.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.610
So, we're looking back
on the year's best shows,

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.280
on this week's Binge Guide.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.560
If there is one silver lining
to the garbage fire of a year,

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.530
that was 2020, it was the
incredible slate of TV

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.040
and streaming shows that occupied

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.570
our couch-filled days at home,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.030
and while there were
plenty of contenders for

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.030
the best of the year,

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.170
we think this list will leave you

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.448
happily bingeing well into 2021.

00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:26.200
So, in no particular order here
are our best shows of 2020.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.270
Starting with "The Queen's Gambit"

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.240
This chest centric limited series

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.210
was a smash hit for Netflix,

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.770
and features in addictive story,

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.040
captivating dialogue,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.900
and stylish art direction that
make for a compelling watch

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.550
from start to finish that's
really hard not to binge.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.130
With a 99% Tomatometer score,

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.120
critics and audiences praise the show

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.950
for star Anya Taylor Joy's
magnetic performance,

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.510
and calling the show an absolute win.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.620
Bingeing the whole series
takes just seven hours,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.670
which is honestly nothing
compared to the time

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.080
that you'll spend playing
chess, after watching it.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:57.922
Next on our list is the FX series,

00:00:57.922 --> 00:01:00.800
"What We Do In The Shadows"

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.760
Based on the 2014 film of the same name,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.900
this horror mockumentary

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.930
from Taika Waititi and Jemaine Clement,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.450
follows a group of vampires

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.130
living together in Staten Island,

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.630
which is way more
hilarious than it sounds.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.370
The second season builds on
the good will from the first,

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.170
and has been given unanimous praise,

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.780
with 10 Emmy nominations,

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.860
and a 100% on the Tomatometer,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.060
with critics saying it "savvily expands

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.430
its supernatural horizons,

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.060
while doubling down on the fast flying fun."

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.810
With 20 episodes total,

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.450
you can binge both
seasons in about 10 hours,

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.760
which is like a blink of an eye

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.690
when you live forever like a vampire.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.127
Another 2020 breakout worth bingeing is

00:01:37.127 --> 00:01:38.560
"I May Destroy you"

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.540
Co-produced by HBO and BBC,

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.680
this comedy drama explores sexual assault

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.240
and modern dating using a blend

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.990
of carefully crafted storylines

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.730
and ultra believable characters

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.810
that infuse humanity and a surprising

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.530
amount of levity into an
otherwise dark subject.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.170
Star Michaela Coel's undeniable talent

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.890
is on full display in front
and behind the camera,

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.770
as she co-directed eight
episodes in the first season,

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.950
which critics called "brave and delicate"

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.770
in its ability to balance dark humor,

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.620
with moments of deep discomfort.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.240
And at an easy half hour each,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.780
you can binge all 12 episodes

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.520
of the series in just around six hours.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.970
Next up is another one of
our returning favorites,

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.670
"The Boys"

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.010
After a killer first season,

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.380
Amazon's atypical superhero
series returned in 2020

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.290
with more irreverent action,

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.390
jaw-dropping violence,

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.300
and timely societal commentary

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.950
as our ragtag group of
heroes continued their fight,

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.060
against the corporate created supes.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.480
Critics called the second season "superb",

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.970
praising the show's ability
to "up the action ante

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.220
without pulling socially critical punches."

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.210
You can watch the entire
series in about 16 hours,

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.180
and if you can get through
it all in one sitting,

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.770
then you can call
bingeing your superpower.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.870
And rounding out our list

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.740
is one of the funniest
shows ever, "Schitt's Creek"

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.592
This comedy series created

00:02:51.592 --> 00:02:54.040
by and starring Dan and Eugene Levy

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.570
about a wealthy family who's
forced to move to a town

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.560
that they purchased as a joke

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.760
made history when it's
six and final season

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.350
swept the comedy categories

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.970
at the Emmy's a first for any genre.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:08.550
And with a Certified Fresh
Tomatometer score of a 100%,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.030
critics called the final season,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.460
"witty, warm, and a fitting farewell."

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.290
You can binge all six seasons
of Schitt's in 28 hours,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.840
and then you'll have nothing
but hilarious one-liners,

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.304
and Moira's accent stuck in your head.

00:03:20.304 --> 00:03:21.170
EW, DAVID!

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.530
All right friends, hopefully this list

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.800
will keep you bingeing
well into the new year.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.230
Did your favorite make our list?

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.990
Let us know in the comments.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:28.910
And be sure to check out

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.340
the new Rotten Tomatoes Is Wrong

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.880
a Podcast from Rotten Tomatoes,

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:32.890
because Fresh and Rotten

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.560
is just the beginning of the conversation,

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.050
and new episodes drop every Thursday,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.750
We hope to see you guys back here

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.850
for more recommendations
based around the movies,

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.470
and shows that you love right here

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.421
on the Rotten Tomatoes Binge Guide.

00:03:44.421 --> 00:03:47.004
(upbeat music)

